---
const features = [
  {
    title: "Learn on demand. Search on every scan.",
    description:
      "Learning is expensive and unpredictable, searching cheap and deterministic — so the agent learns the code on demand, the engine searches it on every scan, and the security review becomes lean and continuous.",
  },
  {
    title: "Enact what the agent learns.",
    description:
      "Vulnerability patterns become readable AST-pattern taint rules that define forbidden dataflow traces. Code behavior becomes dataflow summaries that let the engine trace through code it never analyzed.",
  },
  {
    title: "Fast scans. Fewer false alarms. Fewer missed findings.",
    description:
      "OpenTaint is built to hold all three corners of the classic static-analysis trilemma. Its formal inter-procedural dataflow analysis tracks tainted values across procedures, fields, aliases, async code, and persistence layers at scale.",
  },
  {
    title: "Open source, customizable, and self-hosted.",
    description:
      "Engine, AST-pattern rules, agent skills, and CI integrations ship under Apache 2.0 and MIT — an AI-ready open source alternative to Semgrep Pro and CodeQL.",
  },
];
---

<section class="band band-tint" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <h2 id="what-heading" class="section-title text-center">What is OpenTaint?</h2>
    <p class="subheadline">
      The open source taint analysis engine for the AI era. A formal dataflow analysis tool you can customize and self-host, built so AI agents drive your application security analysis without burning tokens on every scan. AI-ready open source alternative to Semgrep Pro and CodeQL.
    </p>

    <h2 id="why-heading" class="section-title mt-12 lg:mt-14 text-center">Why is OpenTaint?</h2>
    <p class="subheadline">
      During a security review, the agent turns what it learns into reusable analysis artifacts. OpenTaint applies them deterministically across the whole codebase and every future commit.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-left lg:mt-10 lg:space-y-5">
      {features.map((feature) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 font-mono text-[15px] leading-[185%] lg:text-base lg:gap-4">
          <span class="mt-[0.65em] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <strong class="feature-title">{feature.title}</strong>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">{feature.description}</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>

</section>
